Debug.Assert(OLD(this.Count) - OLD(_items.Length) <= x && x <= this.Count - OLD(_items.Length) + OLD(this._size));
</code>
I'll interpret the comment as meaning that the count of the list decreases by an amount between 0 and the difference between the current size and the current capacity. This count difference is between the current size (Count) and the old size (_old_size), where _old_size is the count at the beginning of the function. In the context of array doubling, if an array is increased by 2 in size, the old count could be twice the new count, but never less than.
